<p>There are a few things that need to be made clear here</p>

<ul>
  <li>mas_makeConstraints is a method Masonry extends for NSArray, used for batch processing of views. It requires NSArray.count &gt; 1</li>
  <li>The uniform layout here implements a fixed size. If you need multiple views of different sizes, this approach doesn’t apply</li>
  <li>Masonry doesn’t have the declarative programming found in ArkUI and SwiftUI, with container alignment like start, center, end. That’s why you see code like the following</li>
</ul>

